# FCPL 2026 Player Profile Showcase

This package contains a browser-based player profile gallery created from the verified registration workbook. It requires no software installation.

## Included
- Player gallery with search and filters
- Individual full player profile
- Full-screen profile showcase with Previous/Next controls
- Status selection: Available, Sold, Unsold, Withdrawn
- Team dropdown when recording allocation
- Sold price field
- Browser-based saving
- Export/import backup of allocation results

## Files to upload to GitHub
Upload these four files to the repository root:
- index.html
- styles.css
- app.js
- data.js

README.md is only an instruction file.

## Set the actual team names
1. On GitHub, open data.js.
2. Click the pencil icon to edit.
3. Go to the bottom of the file.
4. Replace Team 1, Team 2, etc. with the actual team names.
5. Keep the quotation marks, commas and square brackets unchanged.
6. Click Commit changes.

Example:
window.FCPL_TEAMS = ["Tambaram Titans", "Chennai Warriors", "Super Strikers", "Royal Challengers"];

## Publish with GitHub Pages
1. Create a free account at github.com.
2. Create a new PUBLIC repository named fcpl-2026-profiles.
3. Choose Add file > Upload files.
4. Upload index.html, styles.css, app.js and data.js.
5. Click Commit changes.
6. Open Settings > Pages.
7. Under Build and deployment choose Deploy from a branch.
8. Select main and /(root), then Save.
9. Wait 2-10 minutes and use the Pages link shown by GitHub.

## Using the showcase
- Players: browse, search and open any profile.
- Profile showcase: use Previous and Next for a projector presentation.
- Admin: choose a player, status and team, then save.
- Export results: download a JSON backup at the end of every session.
- Import results: restore a previously exported JSON backup.

## Important limitation
Saved status/team changes are stored only in the browser used to make them. Other phones do not receive live updates. Export results before clearing browser data or moving to another laptop.

## Player photographs
Google Drive photographs display only if their source files are shared as Anyone with the link - Viewer. If a photo is unavailable, the website displays the player's initials.

## Privacy
The public data intentionally excludes email, phone number, flat/unit number and registration timestamp.
